  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "Critical and analytical; the document examines an isomorphism claim with rigorous scrutiny, acknowledging both potential and gaps.",
    "Q1_identity": "An isomorphism record (ISO-022) that maps the Lowe Coherence Lagrangian (LLC) to Christian theology's unity of truth and divine simplicity.",
    "Q2_domain": "Physics/Mathematics and Christian Theology; cross-domain analysis.",
    "Q3_claim": "The ten laws of the framework, when expressed as a coupled Lagrangian system with specific symmetry pairs, structurally instantiate the theological claim that all truth is unified under one God.",
    "Q4_support": "Conceptual mapping between Lagrangian mechanics (unity generating multiplicity, Noether's theorem) and theology (divine simplicity, creation, coherence). Evidence from information-entropy duality (Landauer/Shannon) and gravitational phase transitions.",
    "Q5_dependencies": "The LLC must be a genuine Lagrangian (satisfying Euler-Lagrange equations, having defined coordinates and kinetic/potential terms). The symmetry pairs must be mathematically justified, not numbering-dependent.",
    "Q6_consequences": "If confirmed, this ISO provides a formal instantiation of 'all truth is God's truth' and connects all other ISOs. If falsified, it collapses to analogy or notation.",
    "Q7_kill": "Show the LLC is not a real Lagrangian (fails Euler-Lagrange, uses notation without content). Show symmetry pairs are numbering-dependent. Show any ten items can be paired this way. Show divine simplicity does not entail unified physical law (voluntarist theology)."
  },
